%description:

A defect of StochasticChannelModel::rayleighFading(), recorded rather than
fixed: every link on a band fades by the same value.

Small-scale fading is a property of a link -- of the scatterers between two
particular antennas -- so the fading of two different links is two
independent random variables. With a continuous distribution, two independent
realizations differ on every band with probability 1.

rayleighFading(id, band) ignores the link: it returns the band-th entry of the
one table PhyPisaData fills at the Binder's construction, so every node, and
every link of every node, sees the same value on a band. Configurations that
select fadingType = RAYLEIGH (channelmodel Rayleigh-38901, for one) therefore
fade all their links in lockstep.

ChannelModelJakesFading pins what the function does today, so that any change
to it fails there by name; when the fading is per link, update that pin and
drop the %expected-failure line here.

%expected-failure: Rayleigh fading is one value per band shared by every link

%includes:
#include "SchedulerTestUtil.h"
#include "ChannelModelTestUtil.h"

%global:
using namespace simu5g;
using namespace simu5g::unittest;

%file: harness.ned
import simu5g.common.binder.Binder;
import simu5g.stack.phy.medium.CellularRadioMedium;
import simu5g.common.carrierAggregation.CarrierAggregation;
import simu5g.stack.phy.channelmodel.Tr38901ChannelModel;

network Harness
{
    submodules:
        binder: Binder;
        radioMedium: CellularRadioMedium;
        carrierAggregation: CarrierAggregation;
        bsChannelModel: Tr38901ChannelModel;
        test: Test;
}

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
network = Harness
cmdenv-express-mode = false
cmdenv-log-prefix = ""
sim-time-limit = 1s

*.carrierAggregation.numComponentCarriers = 1
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].carrierFrequency = 3.5GHz
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].numBands = 10
**.cellInfoModule = ""
*.binder.printTrafficGeneratorConfig = false

# The fading parameters, stated rather than inherited.
**.fading = true
**.fadingType = "RAYLEIGH"

%no-default-inifile: 1

%activity:
Checker c;
auto *bs = harnessModule<StochasticChannelModel>(this, "bsChannelModel");
StubEndpoint bsEndpoint;
bs->setPhy(&bsEndpoint);
const int bands = bs->getNumBands();

// Two links of the base station, to two different UEs.
int sameBands = 0;
for (int band = 0; band < bands; band++)
    if (bs->rayleighFading(MacNodeId(1025), band) == bs->rayleighFading(MacNodeId(1026), band))
        sameBands++;
c.check("two different links fade independently: different values on every band", sameBands == 0,
        std::to_string(sameBands) + " of " + std::to_string(bands) + " bands identical");

c.summary();

%contains: stdout
modelchecks=1 modelfailures=0

%not-contains: stdout
FAILED
